Z||000000||bilbo||02-07-2001||10:34 AM||||DOES ANYONE HAVE A COMPUTER CHECKING DEVICE THAT YOU CAN HOOK UP TO THE FIERO?KIND OF LIKE A DIAGNOSTIC CHECK THAT READS THE CODES.I'M LOOKING TOO GET ONE BUT I FIGURED I'D ASK YOU GUY'S FIRST.WHERE'D YOU GET IT,PRICE,EASY TO USE AND READ??!!THANKS  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-07-2001||10:40 AM||||First off, all CAPS is considered yelling!  Just a reminder.<P>A trouble code is set in the computer anytime the service engine light comes on.  To get these codes out of the computer, you need to remove the cigarette lighter bezel, turn the ignition on, and jumper the two terminals on the ALDL (assembly line diagnostics link).  It is the little black connector facing outward.  Once it is jumpered, watch the engine light.  It will flash once, and then twice, and it will do that 3 times.  (This is code 12, 1 flash + 2 flash = Code 12)  Trouble codes will now be displayed, in the same flashing manner, in numerical order, not in the order that they were set.  All codes will be flashed 3 times.  When the computer is done displaying codes, it will flash code 12 again.<P>Hope this helps, it is for sure a lot cheaper than buying a scantool.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||bilbo||02-07-2001||10:49 AM||||THATS TOO MUCH OF A PAIN IN THE A$$.I WANT SOMETHING FAIRLY CHEAP THAT I CAN HOOK UP AND IT TELLS ME EXACTLY WHAT CODE IS OFF.NONE OF THIS PAPERCLIP STUFF.I'M YELLING TOO MAKE SURE I'M HEARD!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||02-07-2001||10:49 AM||||Run out and buy a Haynes manual, the entire procedure is described therein also suggested cures for the various codes. If you own a Fiero you will eventually need some sort of repair manual.||||reg||1
